{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_142757_f20148", "exit_code": 0, "text": "**Email 1: Awareness**\n\nSubject: Reducing cloud workstation costs without losing performance\n\nHi Morgan,\n\nYour engineers need powerful tools for CAD and AI work. Cloud workstations handle heavy tasks, but monthly fees add up across a 400-person firm.\n\nLocal AI capability can reduce that recurring cost while keeping client data under your control. The Aurora 14 AI Workstation runs open-weight language models up to 30 billion parameters directly on the device. Engineers can work on-site where connectivity is unreliable, without waiting for cloud sync.\n\nThis approach also simplifies fleet management. Fewer device types mean predictable service and easier upgrades.\n\nCan I send you a brief comparison of local versus cloud workstation costs for your team size?\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]\n\n---\n\n**Email 2: Cloud-first objection**\n\nSubject: Aurora 14 specs for cloud-first teams\n\nHi Morgan,\n\nI understand your team relies on cloud workstations. The question is whether local capability complements that investment.\n\nThe Aurora 14 includes a Helix H9 AI processor with an integrated NPU rated at 60 TOPS. It runs AI models on-device in configurations with 64 GB of memory or more. The Vireo V8000 Pro discrete GPU with 16 GB of dedicated graphics memory handles CAD and simulation locally.\n\nSecurity features include a fingerprint reader, IR camera, TPM 2.0, and self-healing BIOS. Memory and storage are user-upgradeable through two SO-DIMM slots and two M.2 slots.\n\nThis means engineers can work offline on client drawings, then sync when connectivity returns. Cloud workstations remain for peak loads, but daily tasks shift locally.\n\nWould you like to see how the 3-year on-site warranty fits your service expectations?\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]\n\n---\n\n**Email 3: Meeting request**\n\nSubject: 15 minutes before Q1 budget closes\n\nHi Morgan,\n\nYour budget cycle closes at the end of Q1. If local AI workstations make sense for your team, approval needs to happen now.\n\nI can walk you through:\n- Total cost comparison versus current cloud workstation spend\n- How the Aurora 14 fits your existing fleet management\n- Security controls that keep client data under your control\n- Availability timing for Q4 deployment\n\nNo pressure to decide today. Just a factual review so you have options before the cycle closes.\n\nAre you available for 15 minutes next Tuesday or Wednesday morning?\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]", "tokens": {"input": 4666, "output": 534, "total": 5200, "cache_read": 0, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 9198, "timestamp": 1790803687148}